{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu22", "cards": [{"id": "u2.t.adaptation", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ad<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ap<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TA<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"adaptation\" data-audio=\"audio/adaptation.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: adaptation\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"adaptation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Trait<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">thick waxy skin on<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">a cactus<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Benefit<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">holds water in a<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">dry desert<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An inherited trait that helps an organism survive and reproduce in its environment.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>适应<\/b>：帮助生物在其环境中生存和繁殖的遗传性状。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">adapt = fit to. An adaptation fits a body to its home.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">adapt = 使适合：让身体适合其环境。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is a giraffe stretching its neck an adaptation?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. An adaptation is an inherited trait, not a behaviour done in one lifetime.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.selective-pressure", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">se<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LEC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tive<\/span> <span class=\"st\">PRES<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sure<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"selective pressure\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: selective pressure\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"selective pressure\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Predators<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">or drought<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">or disease<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Some<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">survive<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Their<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">traits<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">spread<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An environmental factor that affects which individuals survive and reproduce.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>选择压力<\/b>：影响哪些个体能存活并繁殖的环境因素。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">pressure pushes the population in one direction.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">pressure = 把种群推向某个方向。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Name one selective pressure.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Predators, disease, food shortage, climate change, and so on.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.competition", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">com<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">pe<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"competition\" data-audio=\"audio/competition.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: competition\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"competition\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"14\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"50\" r=\"14\" class=\"f2\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"36\" width=\"20\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><line x1=\"66.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"50.0\"/><polygon points=\"88.0,50.0 83.5,52.2 83.5,47.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"134.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"112.0\" y2=\"50.0\"/><polygon points=\"112.0,50.0 116.5,47.8 116.5,52.2\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">two species, one food<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">When organisms use the same limited resource, such as food, water or space.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>竞争<\/b>：生物争夺同一种有限资源，如食物、水或空间。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">com- = together, petere = seek. Seek the same thing.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">com- = 一起，petere = 追求：追求同一样东西。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why does competition lead to selection?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Not everyone gets enough, so the better-suited individuals survive and reproduce more.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.microevolution", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">mi<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cro<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ev<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LU<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"microevolution\" data-audio=\"audio/microevolution.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: microevolution\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"microevolution\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"100\" class=\"\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"40\" width=\"25\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"55\" width=\"25\" height=\"45\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"70\" width=\"25\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"8.79120879120879\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">allele frequency falls over generations<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">one population, small change<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Small changes in allele frequencies within one population over a few generations.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>微观演化<\/b>：种群内等位基因频率在几代之间发生的小变化。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">micro = small.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">micro = 小。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is a change in allele frequencies in one population micro- or macroevolution?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Microevolution.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.macroevolution", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">mac<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ro<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ev<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LU<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"macroevolution\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: macroevolution\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"macroevolution\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"110\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"64\" y2=\"35\"/><line x1=\"64\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"64\" y2=\"60\"/><line x1=\"64\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"10\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"13\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">lizard<\/text><line x1=\"64\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"60\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bird<\/text><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"110\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mouse<\/text><line x1=\"2\" y1=\"72.5\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"72.5\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Large changes over long time, such as the origin of new species and major groups.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>宏观演化<\/b>：经历很长时间的大变化，如新物种和大类群的起源。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">macro = large.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">macro = 大。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is the origin of a new species micro- or macroevolution?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Macroevolution.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.speciation", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">spe<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ci<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">A<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"speciation\" data-audio=\"audio/speciation.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: speciation\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"speciation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">One<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">species<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Groups<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">kept<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">apart<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Two<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">species<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The formation of a new species from an existing one.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>物种形成<\/b>：从已有物种中形成新物种的过程。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">species + -ation = making species.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">species + -ation = 形成物种。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is speciation?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">One species splitting into two or more new species.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.reproductive-isolation", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">re<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">pro<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">DUC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tive<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">i<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">so<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LA<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"reproductive isolation\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: reproductive isolation\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"reproductive isolation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"18\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"50\" r=\"18\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"80\" class=\"k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">no interbreeding<\/text><text x=\"50\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">group 1<\/text><text x=\"150\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">group 2<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A barrier that stops two groups from mating or from producing fertile offspring.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>生殖隔离<\/b>：使两个群体无法交配、或无法产生可育后代的屏障。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">isolate comes from Latin insula = island: cut off like an island.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">isolate 来自拉丁语 insula（岛）：像孤岛一样被隔开。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does reproductive isolation prevent?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Gene flow between groups, because they cannot interbreed successfully.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.geographic-isolation", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ge<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">GRAPH<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ic<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">i<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">so<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LA<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"geographic isolation\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: geographic isolation\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"geographic isolation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M10 70 L50 20 L90 70 Z\" class=\"f7\"/><path d=\"M110 70 L150 20 L190 70 Z\" class=\"f7\"/><circle cx=\"25\" cy=\"85\" r=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"175\" cy=\"85\" r=\"8\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mountain barrier<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">one population split in two<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A physical barrier, such as a river or mountain range, that separates populations.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>地理隔离<\/b>：河流、山脉等自然屏障把种群分隔开。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">geo = earth, graph = write/map. Separated on the map.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">geo = 地，graph = 图：在地图上被分开。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Name an example of geographic isolation.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">A new river, a mountain range or a stretch of ocean separating populations.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.adaptive-radiation", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">a<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">DAP<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tive<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">ra<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">di<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">A<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"adaptive radiation\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: adaptive radiation\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"adaptive radiation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"30\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"25\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"25\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"30\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">finch A<\/text><text x=\"70\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">finch B<\/text><text x=\"130\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">finch C<\/text><text x=\"170\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">finch D<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Fast formation of many new species from one ancestor, each filling a different niche.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>适应辐射<\/b>：从一个祖先在较短时间内分化出许多新物种，各占不同生态位。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">radiation = rays spreading out from a centre (like the sun).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">radiation = 像阳光一样从中心向外散开。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Which famous example of adaptive radiation lives on the Galapagos?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Darwin&#x27;s finches.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.convergent-evolution", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">con<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">VER<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gent<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">ev<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LU<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"convergent evolution\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: convergent evolution\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"convergent evolution\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Shark (fish)<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">streamlined body,<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fins<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"10.491071428571427\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Dolphin (mammal)<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">streamlined body,<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">flippers<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Unrelated groups evolve similar traits because they face similar environments.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>趋同演化<\/b>：亲缘关系远的类群因环境相似而演化出相似的特征。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">con- = together, verge = turn toward. Different roads, same place.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">convergent = 汇聚：不同路径，相同结果。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Sharks and dolphins look alike but are not close relatives. What process explains this?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Convergent evolution.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u2.t.adaptation", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An inherited trait that helps an organism survive and reproduce in its environment.”<\/i>", "opts": ["adaptation", "reproductive isolation", "mutation", "analogous structure"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>adaptation<\/b>: An inherited trait that helps an organism survive and reproduce in its environment. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">适应<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.selective-pressure", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An environmental factor that affects which individuals survive and reproduce.”<\/i>", "opts": ["analogous structure", "heritable trait", "selective pressure", "fossil"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>selective pressure<\/b>: An environmental factor that affects which individuals survive and reproduce. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">选择压力<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.competition", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“When organisms use the same limited resource, such as food, water or space.”<\/i>", "opts": ["analogous structure", "natural selection", "microevolution", "competition"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>competition<\/b>: When organisms use the same limited resource, such as food, water or space. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">竞争<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.microevolution", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Small changes in allele frequencies within one population over a few generations.”<\/i>", "opts": ["microevolution", "coevolution", "analogous structure", "selective pressure"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>microevolution<\/b>: Small changes in allele frequencies within one population over a few generations. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">微观演化<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.macroevolution", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Large changes over long time, such as the origin of new species and major groups.”<\/i>", "opts": ["fitness", "macroevolution", "competition", "comparative embryology"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>macroevolution<\/b>: Large changes over long time, such as the origin of new species and major groups. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">宏观演化<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.speciation", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“The formation of a new species from an existing one.”<\/i>", "opts": ["genetic drift", "bottleneck effect", "speciation", "sexual selection"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>speciation<\/b>: The formation of a new species from an existing one. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物种形成<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.reproductive-isolation", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A barrier that stops two groups from mating or from producing fertile offspring.”<\/i>", "opts": ["sexual selection", "coevolution", "mass extinction", "reproductive isolation"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>reproductive isolation<\/b>: A barrier that stops two groups from mating or from producing fertile offspring. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">生殖隔离<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.geographic-isolation", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A physical barrier, such as a river or mountain range, that separates populations.”<\/i>", "opts": ["vestigial structure", "molecular evidence", "homologous structure", "geographic isolation"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>geographic isolation<\/b>: A physical barrier, such as a river or mountain range, that separates populations. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">地理隔离<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.adaptive-radiation", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Fast formation of many new species from one ancestor, each filling a different niche.”<\/i>", "opts": ["sexual selection", "adaptive radiation", "antibiotic resistance", "adaptation"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>adaptive radiation<\/b>: Fast formation of many new species from one ancestor, each filling a different niche. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">适应辐射<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.convergent-evolution", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Unrelated groups evolve similar traits because they face similar environments.”<\/i>", "opts": ["convergent evolution", "evolution", "antibiotic resistance", "homologous structure"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>convergent evolution<\/b>: Unrelated groups evolve similar traits because they face similar environments. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">趋同演化<\/span>", "whys": null}]}